      looks at one thing and two things are two questions (D38), recorded as a gap to fill;
    - split into two questions, each judged, as D38 says;
    - do not judge such a topic until Step 1 opens it as one thing.
  - Alex: "只判主要那件 (Recommended)".
- **Decided:**
  - In the clean Step 4's ladder step, a thesis gets at most one judged question: the part its `outcome` names. Every other part of
    its wording is listed and shown beside the answer as not judged.
  - A thesis with no main part gets no judged question, with the reason recorded.
  - For a topic that holds two real bets this departs from D38 until splitting is built. It is an open defect, sized by the first
    test: readers mark each part left out as a bet an analyst would hold or not.
- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step only. D38 stands for production.



## D403 · 2026-11-10 · An event's due day is a stated date or the last day of the thesis's period; the model picks no other day

- **Asked:** "事件类问题（比如“监管机构会不会批准这笔收购”）的到期日怎么定？我现在的设计只允许取两种日子：文章或题目里写明的日期，或题目所说期间的最后一天；模型不能自己估一个日子。这比老系统的说法更严（老系统只说“写明这件事在哪一天评定”）。你同意吗？"
  - Options: keep it narrower (recommended): the day comes from the period Step 1 set, the same thesis gets the same day on every
    send, and a reader can check it; the cost is that an event with no date in the article and no period in the thesis is
    declined. Or production's wider sentence: the model judges when the matter will be settled and sets a day; more flexible, and
    three sends of one thesis may set three days.
  - Alex: "保持更严 (Recommended)".
- **Decided:** on the clean path's ladder step, an event's due day is the date the thesis or the article gives, or the last day of
  the period the thesis names (the company's current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision with no date, as v74i line
  16 has it). The model chooses no other day; an event that gives neither is declined as "nothing in the topic can be checked on
  a date". This is narrower than v74i line 26 by his decision.
- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step. Production's frozen sentence is unchanged.



## D436 · 2026-11-13 · One bet seen from two sides is one question; change 3 is dropped; G1-a and G1-b run without it

- **Asked**, after two blind source readers agreed on none of six cases (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/PREREAD-RESULT.md`):
  "例子：同一篇文章里有'2027 年 HBM 出货增长多少'和'2027 年 HBM 是否仍然供不应求'。两位读者对照原文判：一位说这是两个能分别押注的题，另一位说是同一件事的两面，放一张卡就够。…你怎么看：这类情况应该算一个题还是两个题？"
  - Options: one question, change 3 dropped (recommended): "第二件事作为同一题的背景留着（后面判断时显示为'不判'），第三处改动作废。理由：都是同一个押注的不同侧面；我们的原则是偏谨慎、不要把一件事拆成碎题。"; two questions, change 3 continues; case by case.
  - Alex: "算一个题，第三处不改 (Recommended)".
- **Asked:** "第三处停下后，这两处的小测试（42 次发送，约 0.6 美元，上限 2 美元）要不要照常跑？" Options: run (recommended): "这两处不依赖第三处。任何一项不过就停，报给你。"; wait. Alex: "照常跑 (Recommended)".
- **Decided:** a second side of the same bet (the shortage beside the shipments, the AI-chip share beside the chip total, the capacity keeping pace beside the demand) is one question; it stays as context in that question and is shown as not judged (D397). Change 3 (the `outcome` definition) is dropped, and the "two bets in one thesis" class is closed as not a Step 1 defect under this ruling. G1-a and G1-b run as fixed in `COMBINED-PLAN.md`; the candidate for later gates is c8 with changes 1 and 2 only.
- **Scope:** clean Step 1; c8 stays in force.



codex
**The revised closing matches the system text and schema, but all three can still ask for an answer choice to be listed as “not judged.”** For example, “Will the acquisition close?” leaves withdrawal out of the question’s wording, even though the answer choices can already decide whether the parties withdrew.

| Instruction | Verdict against the cited decisions |
|---|---|
| Ask one figure for a named period or one event; judge what the topic’s outcome names as tracked. | **Consistent** with D397. It adds no rule giving the description priority. |
| Read the description and outcome together; list every other part **the question leaves out**. The schema repeats this. | **Keeps wider** than D397’s purpose when “leaves out” is read literally: an answer choice can decide something that the question itself does not name. |
| Keep a second side of the same bet as context and list it as not judged. | **Consistent** with D436. Its examples do not establish which side is main in every case. |
| A second side alone is no reason to decline; decline if no part is main or the main part meets a decline case. | **Consistent** with D436 and D397. It does not introduce the refused description-priority rule. |
| Do not combine two things into one set of answer choices; list the omitted part in the examples. | **Consistent** with D397, provided the omitted part is not already decided by the answer choices. |
| Decline when nothing can be checked on a date, including an undated event with no named period, subject to the regulatory exception. | **Consistent** with D403. |
| Decline when there is no main part; decline another company’s figure or a matter no listed theme covers. | **Consistent** with D397 on no main part. **No source** for the company and theme boundaries in the three cited decisions; they are retained from the frozen request. |
| The other period and year decline cases, and the rule against rewriting a distant-year figure as an event. | **No source** in the three cited decisions; retained from the frozen request. |
| List a difference within an event outcome, such as approval with versus without conditions. | **Consistent** with D397 when the answer choices do not decide that difference. |
| Revised closing: check every other part **the question leaves out**. | **Consistent with the system text and schema; it adds nothing beyond them.** It also repeats their ambiguity about parts the answer choices already decide. |

Two equally presented years with no main one still meet the explicit decline instruction. Another company’s figure and a matter without a listed theme also still have explicit decline instructions. A model could misapply “second side” to any of these, but the text does not expressly override those boundaries. As the earlier audit found, the sources do not settle how to choose a main part when several candidates are named.

NOT SOUND: “The question leaves out” can include event alternatives already decided by the answer choices.
